From 32bb8298dc5e76df1d60727dad29d8512525f28e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:55:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] A player's hunter the GM revives from the fight's card
 stands up at 1 HP on the player's phone too

The cause: Revive had two paths. The GM board's raised the row and posted the room's revive in one write; the card's
went to the life machine only for this phone's hunter, and for a player's hunter only raised the row, so the player
got the fight's totals, which a dead sheet does not take (vitals.ts TABLE.dead.setHp), and stayed dead while the GM's
row stood at 1 HP. Now combat.js `revive` is the one Revive of a down row, for the card and the board: this phone's
hunter's life through hunter.life, a player's always as the room's revive with its log line in the raise's write
(the player's sheet takes it only while dead), any other row raised to 1 HP. gm.js asks it in place of building the
fight half itself. Audit BUG-views-3; held by the two revive cases of tests/e2e/table-turn.e2e.ts.
